diff --git a/tools/gogen/README.md b/tools/gogen/README.md
index 3b80057..25e022b 100644
--- a/tools/gogen/README.md
+++ b/tools/gogen/README.md
@@ -1756,3 +1756,21 @@ private instance attributes. The static owned fixture checks constructor
 initialization, snapshots, section reads, stores, self-append and reset between
 test classes. Friend pools and reference actuals keep string storage. The
 generated 16-page equal-length store allocates zero bytes.
+
+### cl_http_utility=>decode_base64 (2026-10-25)
+
+`decode_base64` is a host function like `encode_base64` and `encode_x_base64`
+already are: open-abap-core writes its two `@KERNEL` lines, and
+`abap.DecodeBase64` does the work (frontend NATIVE, `go/abap/http_utility.go`).
+The base64 step is the one `decode_x_base64` proved against Node's lenient
+`Buffer.from(s, "base64")`: both alphabets, padding optional and a stop,
+characters outside the alphabet ignored. Then the bytes are read as UTF-8
+the way Node does — the new pure package `go/nodeutf8` (`nodeutf8.Decode`,
+bytes in, text out): every ill-formed sequence becomes exactly one U+FFFD
+at the Unicode maximal subparts, which Node's decoder (the WHATWG encoding
+spec) follows and Go's `utf8` package does not, so the state machine is
+written out. Valid text around malformed bytes is kept, and the result is
+valid UTF-8, so `strlen` counts characters. The vectors in
+`nodeutf8_test.go` and the fixture `ZCL_GOGEN_T_B64DEC` were generated from
+Node 22, not measured on A4H; the JS emitter refuses the host function as
+it refuses the other base64 ones.
